nd codellama/CodeLlama-7b-Python-hf (base, continuation-pretrained). Default gpt2 variant is the 124 M one; gpt2-medium is optional and only used if requested.\", \"Decoding is greedy with do_sample=False, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, max_new_tokens=64, stop on newline or EOS, no length/repetition penalty; this matches the RepoBench paper's published completion protocol.\", \"Cross-file context is the oracle/RepoBench-provided snippets, not retrieved at test time, isolating completion quality from retrieval quality.\", \"Metrics are mean Edit Similarity (primary, 0-100), Exact Match % (secondary), MAELS (tertiary), with bootstrap 10k CI on ES and McNemar test on paired EM.\", \"Eventual target runtime is a single GPU environment with transformers/torch/datasets/huggingface_hub installed and Hub network access; the current sandbox runs no code.\", \"Statistical comparisons are paired at the instance level (same prompt submitted to both models).\", \"GPT-2 truncation policy: keep up to 60 percent of the 1024-token budget for the <cross_file> head, then keep the tail of <file> up to <MASK>; truncation rate is logged as a covariate. A best-effort attempt will be made to byte-for-byte replicate the RepoBench paper's internal handling.\"], \"uncertainties\": [\"Which CodeLlama-7b variant (Python hf vs. Instruct vs. a different code-specialized 7 B such as deepseek-coder-6.7b-instruct or bigcode/starcoder2-7b) should be the code-specialized arm?\", \"Include gpt2-medium (355 M) as a size-up control, or keep the design strictly two-model?\", \"Evaluation slice size: full ~1 k test instances vs. a budgeted subsample (e.g., 200)?\", \"Is Mean Edit Similarity the headline metric, with EM and MAELS as secondary?\", \"Use RepoBench oracle cross-file context only, or also include a retrieved-context arm?\", \"Should the design be portable/run-on-GPU only with an honest feasibility statement, or also include a degraded CPU-only fallback (n_eval <= 50) that could in principle run in a sandbox with packages installed?\"]}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-7d84d501-5225-4223-bc00-2a752be79d00", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "kind": "ActionEvent", "source_event_index": 20}
